{
  "id": "09_dungeon_crawler_2d",
  "title": "Crypt of the Ember Sigil",
  "genre": "2D top-down dungeon crawler / action-RPG",
  "orientation": 0,
  "startScene": "Main",
  "scenes": [
    "Main"
  ],
  "networking": false,
  "ai_assist": false,
  "scripts": [
    "Warden.js",
    "Grunt.js",
    "Ghost.js",
    "Crawler.js",
    "Spit.js",
    "Bolt.js",
    "Fx.js",
    "DeepDelve.js"
  ],
  "controls": {
    "move": "virtual joystick (8-direction)",
    "attack": "action button A (sword arc)",
    "restart": "action button A on the end screen"
  },
  "systems": [
    "level: generated at runtime from an 11-room grammar on a 72x56 tile grid",
    "rendering: 8x8 tile chunks (63 chunk sprites + overlays) instead of 4032 tile objects",
    "collision: wall runs merged into ~200 axis-aligned colliders",
    "enemy AI: melee patrol/chase/attack, a wall-phasing hunter, a ranged kiter",
    "combat: cone sword arcs, hit-stop, knockback via velocity, out-of-combat regeneration",
    "objectives: 3 sigils to claim, waves escalate while they are missing"
  ],
  "engineNotes": {
    "notes": [
      "The tile atlas is Penusbmic's Dungeon_Tileset.png.  The store refuses to guess a grid for opaque art, so the 10x10/16px grid and the specific cells used are declared in game.json and were verified by rendering the atlas with tools/probe_png.py.",
      "Enemies come from the same pack's monster idle frames (4 per monster).  The engine's Animator plays one texture per clip, so the four frames are four assets and the scripts advance them on a timer rather than shipping a fake sheet.",
      "The hero is the High Forest knight (80x96) rather than the dungeon pack's wizard, because the forest pack is the only one in the store with a full run/attack/death set.",
      "There is no 2D lighting or fog in the renderer (Renderer3D owns both), so the level carries no Light component at all: the warm pools around torches and the warden's ember are additive ParticleEmitters.  A Light in a 2D scene would be inert -- which is why one is not declared here."
    ]
  },
